-- title:
--   The combined Vaughan estimate at modulus two
-- statement:
--   For $q\ge4$, $(|a|,q)=1$, $4\alpha=a/q+\beta$, $|\beta|\le q^{-2}$, and cutoffs $40\le U,V<x$ satisfying $UV\le x/4$ and $x\le UV^2$, the smoothed exponential sum over odd indices satisfies
--   $$|S_{\eta_0,2}|\le\frac{x}{2q}\log x\log(2UV/q+4)+0.89(UV+5q/2)(8+\log q)\log(2x)$$
--   $$\quad+\left(0.1\frac{x}{\sqrt q}+0.39\frac{x}{\sqrt{x/q}}\right)\log(x/(UV))\log(Vx/U)+\left(0.55\frac{x}{\sqrt U}+0.78\frac{x}{\sqrt V}\right)\log(x/U).$$
--   This is the estimate before choosing the Section 6 cutoff parameters.
-- source:
--   Terence Tao, Every odd number greater than 1 is the sum of at most five primes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6656, Sections 5 and 6. Original Lean source: Theorems/Thm_TaoFivePrimes_exp_sum_estimate_vaughan_modulus_two_source.lean, lines 9-58.

